WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.112
Let’s walk through RFIs.

00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:04.350
Use an RFI when the team needs a ruling,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.250
clarification, or missing scenario fact.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.675
State one decision-blocking question with enough context to answer,

00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:13.600
and revise the same record if White Cell returns it

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:13.725
.

00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:16.663
On this slide, answer participant questions or return them

00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:19.012
with required clarification notes.

00:00:19.012 --> 00:00:22.262
In practice, keep the answer on the originating RFI

00:00:22.262 --> 00:00:25.575
so the ruling, revision, and history remain connected

00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:25.700
.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.375
When you are ready, use Open RFIs to move

00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:29.762
to the live surface.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.935
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:32.935 --> 00:00:33.110
.
